WEBVTT

1
00:00:17.309 --> 00:00:19.687
When we lose someone
from the neighborhood.

2
00:00:19.770 --> 00:00:21.564
we all feel it.

3
00:00:21.647 --> 00:00:23.250
What I'd like to know
is who the fuck would

4
00:00:23.274 --> 00:00:24.442
do Pat in our own backyard?

5
00:00:25.860 --> 00:00:26.878
Had a little talk with Danny.

6
00:00:26.902 --> 00:00:28.195
Aw. I appreciate that.

7
00:00:28.279 --> 00:00:29.572
It's a little more complicated.

8
00:00:29.655 --> 00:00:31.741
He thinks I gave the order

9
00:00:31.824 --> 00:00:33.367
and you killed Pat Murphy.

10
00:00:33.451 --> 00:00:34.553
If you want to keep him alive.

11
00:00:34.577 --> 00:00:35.817
keep him out of Hell's Kitchen.

12
00:00:35.870 --> 00:00:38.122
You're asking me
to use federal pull

13
00:00:38.205 --> 00:00:39.832
to ship your kid to a safe house

14
00:00:39.915 --> 00:00:42.209
disguised as a clinic.

15
00:00:42.293 --> 00:00:43.562
I talked to Cahill.
Well. it turns out

16
00:00:43.586 --> 00:00:44.666
he doesn't need the weapon.

17
00:00:44.712 --> 00:00:46.714
I'm sorry. Brendan.
It's gone.

18
00:00:46.797 --> 00:00:48.215
But he does need me.

19
00:00:48.299 --> 00:00:50.384
My target.
Colonel Gerald Markham.

20
00:00:50.468 --> 00:00:51.844
The man who killed your parents.

21
00:00:51.927 --> 00:00:53.304
This is fucking dangerous.

22
00:00:53.387 --> 00:00:54.847
And what you do isn't?

23
00:00:54.930 --> 00:00:57.725
I took six kilos from that disco
before we burned it down.

24
00:00:57.808 --> 00:00:59.560
But if we don't deal it.
someone else will.

25
00:00:59.643 --> 00:01:02.062
and they'll just become stronger
and more of a threat to us.

26
00:01:02.146 --> 00:01:03.397
I think it's worth the risk.

27
00:01:03.481 --> 00:01:05.357
We don't deal drugs.

28
00:01:05.441 --> 00:01:06.668
I can't believe
we're back to this

29
00:01:06.692 --> 00:01:08.235
nickel and dime shit.

30
00:01:08.319 --> 00:01:12.239
Your Mr. Sweeney
just donated $100.000!

31
00:01:12.323 --> 00:01:13.603
You think Sweeney sold our coke?

32
00:01:13.657 --> 00:01:15.242
Fuck yeah. I do.

33
00:01:15.326 --> 00:01:17.495
Eamon Sweeney
with six fucking keys.

34
00:01:17.578 --> 00:01:19.288
-How much?
-Give you 40 apiece

35
00:01:19.371 --> 00:01:21.664
for the first five.
35 for everything after that.

36
00:01:21.749 --> 00:01:24.585
Eamon Sweeney himself
sold it to Leon?

37
00:01:24.668 --> 00:01:26.587
-That's right.
-So. what's our next move?

38
00:01:26.670 --> 00:01:28.464
Kill that motherfucker
Eamon Sweeney.

39
00:01:30.424 --> 00:01:32.426
I just can't believe
he lied to my fucking face.

40
00:01:32.509 --> 00:01:34.845
Problem is.
you put Sweeney on a pedestal.

41
00:01:34.929 --> 00:01:36.263
We all did.

42
00:01:36.347 --> 00:01:37.824
To Eamon Sweeney.
for always looking out

43
00:01:37.848 --> 00:01:39.642
for the less fortunate.
But now we know

44
00:01:39.725 --> 00:01:41.268
he don't fucking belong there.

45
00:01:41.352 --> 00:01:42.728
He has your loyalty. right?

46
00:01:42.812 --> 00:01:44.729
You would die for that
motherfucker. I know you.

47
00:01:47.358 --> 00:01:48.859
You think
he'd say the same for you?

48
00:01:49.610 --> 00:01:51.378
Looks like the Italians
weren't too happy with you

49
00:01:51.402 --> 00:01:52.530
selling that coke.

50
00:01:52.613 --> 00:01:53.613
You wanna get a beer?

51
00:02:27.523 --> 00:02:28.774
You know me. Paul.

52
00:02:28.858 --> 00:02:30.293
I wouldn't have asked
for this sit down

53
00:02:30.317 --> 00:02:32.361
if I didn't think
it was in your best interests.

54
00:02:32.444 --> 00:02:33.821
This guy's threatening war?

55
00:02:33.904 --> 00:02:35.322
I'll send his Irish Mick crew

56
00:02:35.406 --> 00:02:37.741
back to potato land
in a fuckin' box.

57
00:02:37.825 --> 00:02:39.386
Yeah. those
two hitmen you sent after me

58
00:02:39.410 --> 00:02:41.662
are in fuckin' boxes
right now. John.

59
00:02:41.745 --> 00:02:43.664
Happy to make
the same arrangement for you.

60
00:02:43.747 --> 00:02:45.457
Settle down. both of you.

61
00:02:47.251 --> 00:02:48.668
We're here to talk.

62
00:02:51.630 --> 00:02:53.340
You make a move against Eamon?

63
00:02:53.424 --> 00:02:56.218
Of course not. I don't know
anything about this shit.

64
00:02:56.302 --> 00:02:57.678
He used hitmen
from Scarfa's crew.

65
00:02:59.305 --> 00:03:01.640
Angelo Bruno knows
all about it. Ask him.

66
00:03:01.724 --> 00:03:04.518
Who gives a shit what that mopey
motherfucker Angelo Bruno says?

67
00:03:04.602 --> 00:03:06.312
That guy's a fuckin' liar.

68
00:03:06.395 --> 00:03:07.605
Angelo's a boss.

69
00:03:08.981 --> 00:03:11.275
I trust bosses.
How about you. Paul?

70
00:03:14.528 --> 00:03:17.197
This is why I hate drugs. hmm?

71
00:03:17.281 --> 00:03:19.450
Shit like this happens.

72
00:03:19.533 --> 00:03:21.535
You think Angelo Bruno's a liar?

73
00:03:21.619 --> 00:03:23.954
I'll call him
and tell him you said that.

74
00:03:24.038 --> 00:03:26.206
And if Eamon's story
checks out...

75
00:03:26.957 --> 00:03:28.417
you and I will have a problem.

76
00:03:28.500 --> 00:03:30.502
Understand?

77
00:03:30.586 --> 00:03:32.630
Or...

78
00:03:32.713 --> 00:03:34.632
we can agree
to resolve this issue

79
00:03:34.715 --> 00:03:36.634
right here. right now.

80
00:03:38.844 --> 00:03:41.889
Because there's a federal
fucking task force out there

81
00:03:41.972 --> 00:03:44.391
tryin' to put me
in fuckin' jail!

82
00:03:44.475 --> 00:03:46.810
And they're not
interested in you or you.

83
00:03:46.894 --> 00:03:49.772
So I don't want
dead fuckin' bodies piling up

84
00:03:49.855 --> 00:03:51.315
that lead back to me!

85
00:03:51.398 --> 00:03:53.317
Which is why
I don't want neither of you

86
00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:54.567
dealing narcotics!

87
00:03:54.652 --> 00:03:56.654
Can you get that
through your fuckin' heads?

88
00:03:56.737 --> 00:03:58.340
Yeah. you think you're talking
to John right now. right?

89
00:03:58.364 --> 00:03:59.740
Because I don't
fuckin' deal drugs.

90
00:03:59.823 --> 00:04:01.575
Fuck yourself. Sweeney.
Neither do I.

91
00:04:01.659 --> 00:04:03.661
I want you two to make peace.

92
00:04:04.370 --> 00:04:07.247
Whatever your gripes are.
put it behind you.

93
00:04:10.751 --> 00:04:12.795
Eamon Sweeney is
not to be touched.

94
00:04:12.878 --> 00:04:14.713
Or anyone in my crew.

95
00:04:15.464 --> 00:04:16.839
You got that. John?

96
00:04:16.923 --> 00:04:18.759
Not Eamon nor any of his crew.

97
00:04:21.595 --> 00:04:22.846
I can't hear you. John.

98
00:04:24.932 --> 00:04:25.975
Not to be touched.

99
00:04:27.810 --> 00:04:28.978
Good.

100
00:04:36.110 --> 00:04:37.110
Now shake.

101
00:05:01.510 --> 00:05:03.971
-♪ It didn't take long ♪
-♪ It didn't take long ♪

102
00:05:04.054 --> 00:05:06.473
-♪ I didn't get far ♪
-♪ I didn't get far ♪

103
00:05:06.557 --> 00:05:09.518
♪ Before the cops were told ♪

104
00:05:09.601 --> 00:05:12.312
-♪ That I'd stolen the car ♪
-♪ Stolen the car ♪

105
00:05:12.396 --> 00:05:15.065
-♪ There was an APB ♪
-♪ APB ♪

106
00:05:15.149 --> 00:05:17.568
-♪ Sent out for me ♪
-♪ Out for me ♪

107
00:05:17.651 --> 00:05:19.820
♪ Ratted out by my own ♪

108
00:05:19.903 --> 00:05:22.781
♪ Now I'm a public enemy ♪

109
00:05:29.163 --> 00:05:31.915
♪ I'm a Catholic school kid ♪

110
00:05:31.999 --> 00:05:34.960
-♪ I'm an altar boy ♪
-♪ Altar boy ♪

111
00:05:35.044 --> 00:05:37.880
♪ I was dropped on my head ♪

112
00:05:37.963 --> 00:05:40.883
-♪ Now I'm here to destroy ♪
-♪ Here to destroy ♪

113
00:05:40.966 --> 00:05:43.719
-♪ I'm a stone-cold killer ♪
-♪ Stone-cold killer ♪

114
00:05:43.802 --> 00:05:46.513
-♪ In the CYO ♪
-♪ CYO ♪

115
00:05:46.597 --> 00:05:49.099
♪ I'm lining them up ♪

116
00:05:49.183 --> 00:05:51.477
♪ And I'm laying them low ♪

117
00:05:52.436 --> 00:05:54.980
♪ But honest as the day
is long that's a fact ♪

118
00:05:55.064 --> 00:05:58.025
♪ I'm not nearly half
as bad as I act ♪

119
00:05:58.108 --> 00:06:01.487
♪ See. I'm always wrong
in the eyes of the law ♪

120
00:06:01.570 --> 00:06:03.906
♪ Parents and priests say
it's the final straw ♪

121
00:06:03.989 --> 00:06:06.867
♪ But sure as the sun.
it rises and sets ♪

122
00:06:19.880 --> 00:06:21.965
This whiskey was casked in '22.

123
00:06:24.843 --> 00:06:26.053
That's before the Depression.

124
00:06:29.181 --> 00:06:30.724
It's almost as old as I am.

125
00:06:32.601 --> 00:06:34.561
Only 40 cases ever sold.

126
00:06:38.982 --> 00:06:40.734
Oh. Jesus.

127
00:06:40.818 --> 00:06:41.860
That's got quite a kick.

128
00:06:42.986 --> 00:06:45.531
This is liquid bliss.

129
00:06:45.614 --> 00:06:46.966
If you don't mind me saying.
I've had similar reactions

130
00:06:46.990 --> 00:06:48.492
to cough syrup.

131
00:06:50.661 --> 00:06:52.454
I guess it's an acquired taste.

132
00:06:53.914 --> 00:06:55.314
So. I take it
the meeting went well.

133
00:06:56.582 --> 00:06:58.127
Gotti got spanked.

134
00:06:58.210 --> 00:07:00.462
No more narcotics.

135
00:07:00.546 --> 00:07:02.464
but...

136
00:07:02.548 --> 00:07:04.192
Big Paul wants me
to basically ignore the fact

137
00:07:04.216 --> 00:07:06.802
that cocksucker sent
two fuckin' hitmen after me.

138
00:07:06.885 --> 00:07:08.512
Do we go after Gotti?

139
00:07:08.595 --> 00:07:12.599
No. I got a better way
to get that motherfucker back.

140
00:07:12.683 --> 00:07:14.935
He's not allowed
to sell drugs. right?

141
00:07:15.018 --> 00:07:17.187
So... we will.

142
00:07:19.982 --> 00:07:23.527
Okay. Uh. Castellano's
all right with that?

143
00:07:23.610 --> 00:07:24.862
He doesn't have to know.

144
00:07:26.155 --> 00:07:28.740
Look. Jimmy. you were right.

145
00:07:28.824 --> 00:07:30.951
Okay. it makes sense for us
to get into narcotics.

146
00:07:32.161 --> 00:07:33.787
We don't. somebody else will.

147
00:07:33.871 --> 00:07:36.707
they're gonna get richer
and stronger while we stand pat.

148
00:07:36.790 --> 00:07:38.876
Well. you know I agree.

149
00:07:39.710 --> 00:07:41.920
But I stole that coke
from the Colombians

150
00:07:42.004 --> 00:07:44.798
'cause I happened to be there.

151
00:07:44.882 --> 00:07:46.682
I mean. we sure as hell
can't go back to them.

152
00:07:47.718 --> 00:07:49.887
I'm gonna introduce you to Leon.

153
00:07:49.970 --> 00:07:51.847
dude that shylocks for us
up in Harlem.

154
00:07:51.930 --> 00:07:53.015
He can get you supply.

155
00:07:53.098 --> 00:07:55.558
-What about money?
-I'll cover that.

156
00:07:55.642 --> 00:07:58.020
But you gotta do this
on your own. Okay?

157
00:07:58.103 --> 00:08:00.063
I gotta stay on good terms
with Castellano.

158
00:08:00.147 --> 00:08:01.690
Of course.

159
00:08:01.773 --> 00:08:03.859
And ya gotta
be careful. Jimmy.

160
00:08:03.942 --> 00:08:05.944
This cocaine.

161
00:08:06.028 --> 00:08:07.821
it's a nasty fuckin' business.

162
00:08:09.072 --> 00:08:10.782
You can't trust anybody.

163
00:08:13.160 --> 00:08:14.160
Slàinte.

164
00:08:15.370 --> 00:08:16.747
Slàinte.

165
00:08:18.916 --> 00:08:20.751
It's hot as a bitch outside.

166
00:08:20.834 --> 00:08:22.961
and the A/C
in this place is for shit.

167
00:08:23.045 --> 00:08:24.588
Tax dollars at work.

168
00:08:25.964 --> 00:08:27.132
Any word on Danny?

169
00:08:27.216 --> 00:08:28.967
Oh. I hear he's doing fine.

170
00:08:29.051 --> 00:08:30.636
He's only been
disciplined twice.

171
00:08:30.719 --> 00:08:32.011
He hit one of the counselors

172
00:08:32.095 --> 00:08:34.175
and threatened the other one
with cutting her throat.

173
00:08:35.765 --> 00:08:37.934
-I see.
-But let's talk about you!

174
00:08:41.104 --> 00:08:42.856
What about me?

175
00:08:42.940 --> 00:08:45.067
You know. when I invited you
to join this task force.

176
00:08:45.150 --> 00:08:47.694
my superior officers
thought I was crazy.

177
00:08:47.778 --> 00:08:49.655
"He's corrupt." they said.

178
00:08:49.738 --> 00:08:51.865
I said. "So's everybody
at Midtown North."

179
00:08:51.949 --> 00:08:55.535
I said. "You've got to use
a criminal to catch a criminal."

180
00:08:55.619 --> 00:08:58.080
But you. as far as
useful criminals go.

181
00:08:58.163 --> 00:09:00.540
you've been
pretty fuckin' useless!

182
00:09:00.624 --> 00:09:01.904
Does this mean
I'm gettin' fired?

183
00:09:01.959 --> 00:09:05.128
No. it means
you're gonna wear a wire.

184
00:09:05.212 --> 00:09:07.881
What? What.
are you fucking serious?

185
00:09:07.965 --> 00:09:09.258
You tryin' to get me killed?

186
00:09:09.341 --> 00:09:11.551
Get Sweeney on tape
talkin' about something

187
00:09:11.635 --> 00:09:13.720
-we can arrest him for.
-Fuck that. I won't do it.

188
00:09:13.804 --> 00:09:15.806
Then Danny won't get
the help he needs.

189
00:09:16.974 --> 00:09:18.850
I'll have him released.

190
00:09:18.934 --> 00:09:20.894
and he'll be right back
where he started.

191
00:09:22.020 --> 00:09:23.020
You would do that?

192
00:09:24.147 --> 00:09:25.607
Which is it?

193
00:09:30.821 --> 00:09:32.197
You got it?

194
00:09:32.281 --> 00:09:33.281
Yeah. Fine.

195
00:09:37.828 --> 00:09:39.222
You got a lotta tattoos there.

196
00:09:39.246 --> 00:09:40.747
Yeah.

197
00:09:41.915 --> 00:09:44.167
Swift. silent. deadly.

198
00:09:45.210 --> 00:09:47.296
Force Recon motto. right?

199
00:09:47.379 --> 00:09:49.047
Yeah.

200
00:09:49.131 --> 00:09:51.341
Legendary.

201
00:09:51.425 --> 00:09:53.051
I'm betting you were
deep in the shit.

202
00:09:53.135 --> 00:09:54.803
You know. our enemy over there

203
00:09:54.886 --> 00:09:56.281
were a bunch of gooks
I didn't know.

204
00:09:56.305 --> 00:09:57.889
Betraying my friends
is different.

205
00:09:57.973 --> 00:10:00.243
You're working for your country.
same as you were doing then.

206
00:10:00.267 --> 00:10:02.894
Yeah. semantics.

207
00:10:02.978 --> 00:10:05.355
Sweeney's a smart guy.
He won't talk.

208
00:10:05.439 --> 00:10:07.232
It's your job to make him talk.

209
00:10:07.316 --> 00:10:10.944
This guy is
a serious street guy.

210
00:10:11.028 --> 00:10:12.404
not some dipshit novice.

211
00:10:12.487 --> 00:10:14.865
He can spot the fuckin' heat
in a 40-acre field.

212
00:10:16.366 --> 00:10:17.951
Who's his most trusted man?

213
00:10:19.286 --> 00:10:20.787
It's a toss-up
between Eddie Breen

214
00:10:20.871 --> 00:10:22.372
and Dukey Sullivan.
probably Breen.

215
00:10:22.456 --> 00:10:25.125
Tell him Eddie Breen is one
of our confidential informants

216
00:10:25.208 --> 00:10:26.793
and he's been talkin' to me.

217
00:10:26.877 --> 00:10:28.295
No way he'd buy
Breen would talk.

218
00:10:28.378 --> 00:10:30.672
Maybe yes. maybe no...

219
00:10:30.756 --> 00:10:33.300
so plant that seed with care.

220
00:10:33.383 --> 00:10:35.635
I'm gonna hide the recorder
down your pants.

221
00:10:35.719 --> 00:10:37.119
Be careful
when you're sitting down.

222
00:10:42.517 --> 00:10:44.811
This is Colonel Markham.

223
00:10:45.562 --> 00:10:49.107
